<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Toronto-Dominion cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Toronto-Dominion cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Morgan Stanley said it lowered its recommendation on Toronto-Dominion Bank to neutral from outperform.  </p>
<p>-- Analyst Nigel Dally said the lower rating was based on valuation.</p>
<p>-- The 12-month price target was 39 (on the Toronto Stock Exchange), and at 37 &quot;we don't see enough upside to warrant an outperform rating, but the fundamental story is still intact.&quot;</p>
<p>-- He said he made no changes in earnings estimates.</p>
<p>-- Toronto-Dominion's NYSE-listed shares slipped 1/8 to 27-1/4 and the TSE-listed stock slipped 0.10 to 36.60.</p>
</text>
